{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hy1qPaFAdChgDFzwELp8mi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## WI-546 — WI-484 delegated residue: the hats.toml knowledge value-pass and the 17 approved-cell Rationale attribution deletions\n2\t\n3\tSuccessor to WI-484 (drafts-not-mints, R1/R3), scope items **3 and 5 only** of\n4\tWI-484's \"Delegated for the unattended run\" block (SpecRef\n5\t`docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-32`). Item 7 (which traced cells are\n6\tstaleness-bearing) is a classification ruling owed by nobody and is excluded.\n7\tOwner review is at RETURN, not at the act — this session drafts, the owner cuts.\n8\t\n9\t### Item 5 — Phase 4: the `hats.toml` `knowledge` value-pass (FOR OWNER REVIEW)\n10\t\n11\t`hats.py` `OPTIONAL_KEYS` already admits `knowledge` (WI-511); this pass fills\n12\tit. The value-pass is DRAFTED, not ratified — `hats.toml` is owner text, cut at\n13\tRETURN. The existing `docs/knowledge/` packs are research-evidence notes tied to\n14\tcomponents (CMP-006/008), so most did NOT carry a hat's *perspective*; where none\n15\tdid and the hat has a real, repo-grounded perspective body, a new pack was\n16\tdrafted and marked DRAFT in its own header. No path existence is enforced on the\n17\tcell (`hats.py` comment), but every cited pack exists.\n18\t\n19\t**12 hats now carry `knowledge`; 4 stay empty.**\n20\t\n21\tRe-pointed at existing packs (pack subject IS the hat's failure class):\n22\t\n23\t| hat | knowledge |\n24\t|---|---|\n25\t| TEST-ENGINEER | `traceability-enforcement.md` (an enforcer that actually bites) |\n26\t| MAINTAINER | `instruction-file-adherence.md`, `traceability-enforcement.md` (load-bearing vs accident; reason not living only in the authoring session) |\n27\t| FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER | `instruction-file-adherence.md` (a stranger following the shipped instructions/examples) |\n28\t| PERFORMANCE | `prompt-image-token-efficiency.md`, `parallel-scheduling.md` (a size/speed claim measured, or a bound not proven) |\n29\t\n30\tGiven a NEW DRAFT pack (agent-authored, repo-grounded, header-marked DRAFT):\n31\t\n32\t| hat | new pack |\n33\t|---|---|\n34\t| SECURITY | `security-review.md` |\n35\t| UNATTENDED-OPS | `unattended-operation.md` |\n36\t| CROSS-PLATFORM | `cross-platform-scripting.md` |\n37\t| INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY | `crash-atomicity-recovery.md` |\n38\t| UX-DESIGNER, UX-ENGINEER, ACCESSIBILITY | `rendered-surface-review.md` (one shared pack, an angle per hat) |\n39\t| CONSISTENCY | `rendered-surface-review.md` — a PARTIAL fit: the pack covers cross-view coherence (CONSISTENCY's core failure class across the dashboard / open-items / console), but not the template↔instance idiom half of the charter. Owner may want to broaden or split it. |\n40\t\n41\tLeft empty (empty-is-honest — no distinct perspective-knowledge body in this\n42\trepo; documented rather than filled with ceremony):\n43\t\n44\t- **SAFETY, LEGAL, DATA-PROTECTION** — the tag-gated, domain-silent hats. The\n45\t  roster header already flags SAFETY as having \"essentially one reachable\n46\t  referent\" here; a drafted pack would be exactly the ceremony this tier was\n47\t  admitted to prevent.\n48\t- **PRODUCT-FITNESS** — a cross-cutting lens whose knowledge is the charter\n49\t  itself (who asked, does it still serve the need); no separable evidence body.\n50\t\n51\tOwner calls this pass surfaces: (1) keep/cut/rewrite each of the 5 DRAFT packs;\n52\t(2) the 4 empties — draft a pack, gate the hat, or accept empty; (3) the\n53\tCONSISTENCY partial-fit above.\n54\t\n55\t### Item 3 — the 17 approved-cell `Rationale` attribution deletions (FOR OWNER RE-ATTESTATION)\n56\t\n57\tThe WI-484 slice-2 backfill left the deriving-hat attribution stated **twice** —\n58\tonce in the `hat_refs` cell (the record), once in the `Rationale` prose as a\n59\t`Hat-derived (hat.X …)` note. This deletes the prose note; `hat_refs` is\n60\tuntouched and remains the record. **Amendment scope, deliberately narrow:** only\n61\tthe `Hat-derived (…)` attribution note is removed — the hat name(s), any\n62\tclause-id (`C-SEC-2`…) and provenance-doc citation *inside that note*, and the\n63\tcross-hat gloss. The substantive derivation reasoning that followed it is KEPT\n64\t(recapitalised at the join). Clause-ids that sat in the *retained* reasoning were\n65\tleft as-is; Phase 0 already ruled they resolve nowhere, and re-writing them is\n66\tout of this WI's scope.\n67\t\n68\tThese 17 rows are all `Approved`; the amendment proceeds under ordinary review\n69\t(`DevStg-Needs` human-held only), and the snapshot diff against\n70\t`docs/archive/last_approved/` carries the identical set for the re-attestation\n71\tbrief compiled at RETURN. The Phase-5 amend-without-flip guard warns (never\n72\tgates) that a `Rationale` cell moved while `Hat-Refs` stayed put — which is\n73\tEXACTLY what this WI does on purpose: the deletion removes only the duplicate\n74\tattribution, the hats that reach each row are unchanged, and `hat_refs` is\n75\ttherefore correctly left as the record. The guard cannot tell attribution-\n76\tremoval from a substance change, so it fires; \"leave it deliberately\" (the\n77\tguard's own second option) is the right call here, and this fragment is that\n78\trecord. **The two \"poison\" rows SR-015 and SR-040 (both `hat_refs = []`/absent)\n79\tare NOT touched** — their `hat.PERFORMANCE`/`hat.UX-ENGINEER` prose is an argued\n80\t*refusal* of attribution, the record itself, not a duplicate.\n81\t\n82\t| SR | `hat_refs` (unchanged) | prose note removed |\n83\t|---|---|---|\n84\t| SR-024 | TEST-ENGINEER | `Hat-derived (hat.TEST-ENGINEER): ` label |\n85\t| SR-033 | PERFORMANCE | `Hat-derived (hat.PERFORMANCE), and ` label |\n86\t| SR-043 | SECURITY | `Hat-derived (hat.SECURITY): ` label |\n87\t| SR-052 | ACCESSIBILITY | `Hat-derived (hat.ACCESSIBILITY): ` label |\n88\t| SR-053 | CONSISTENCY | `Hat-derived (hat.CONSISTENCY): ` label |\n89\t| SR-054 | UX-DESIGNER, UX-ENGINEER | `Hat